          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              The square on the right is that from Prop.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#G2IsIntersectionOfSpin7SubgroupsInSpin8"}
            %p
              The square in the middle is
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#Varadarajan01"} Varadarajan 01, Lemma 9 on p. 10
            %p
              The statement also follows with
              = succeed ":" do
                %a{:href => "#Onishchik93"} Onishchik 93, Table 2, p. 144
            %div{:style => "text-align: center"}
              %img{:src => "/nlab/files/SO8SubgroupIntersection.jpg", :width => "690px"}/
          %p
            %br/
          %h3#coset_spaces Coset spaces
          #QuotientOfSpin7ByG2IsS7.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coset+space"} coset space
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin%287%29"} Spin(7)
                by
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G%E2%82%82"} G₂
                is
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/7-sphere"} 7-sphere
            %p
              Consider the canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin%287%29"} Spin(7)
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+sphere"} unit sphere
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 8
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^8
              (the
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/7-sphere"} 7-sphere
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  This action is is
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transitive+action"} transitive
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilizer+group"} stabilizer group
                  of any point on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 7
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^7
                  is
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G%E2%82%82"} G₂
              %li
                %p
                  all
                  = succeed "-subgroups" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G%E2%82%82"} G₂
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin%287%29"} Spin(7)
                  arise this way, and are all
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjugate+subgroup"} conjugate
                  to each other.
            %p
              Hence the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coset+space"} coset space
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin%287%29"} Spin(7)
              by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G%E2%82%82"} G₂
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/7-sphere"} 7-sphere
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spin
